📊 Dataset

The project uses a Brazilian travel booking dataset containing:

Flights Dataset
Feature	Description
from	Source city
to	Destination city
flightType	Economic / Premium / First Class
distance	Travel distance
time	Flight duration
agency	Booking agency
price	Flight ticket price
Hotels Dataset

Contains hotel bookings and destination information.

Users Dataset

Contains demographic information such as:

Age
Gender
User ID
🔍 Exploratory Data Analysis

Major insights discovered:

Distance vs Price

Distance showed a strong positive relationship with flight prices.

Flight Type Impact

Price ordering:

First Class > Premium > Economic
Duration Impact

Longer flight durations generally resulted in higher prices.

Agency Analysis

Different booking agencies exhibited different booking patterns and pricing distributions.

Bias Analysis

Gender and age were analyzed to ensure no meaningful pricing bias existed in the dataset.

🤖 Machine Learning Model
Algorithms Evaluated
Linear Regression
Ridge Regression
Random Forest Regressor
XGBoost Regressor
Final Selected Model

✅ Random Forest Regressor

Reasons:

High predictive accuracy
Robust performance
Low error metrics
Stable production behavior
📈 Model Performance

Example performance metrics:

Metric	Score
R² Score	~0.99
MAE	Low
RMSE	Low
⚙️ Feature Engineering

The following features were created:

Day of Week
Month
Route Encoding
Flight Type Encoding
Agency Encoding
Distance Features
Duration Features

Categorical variables were transformed using encoding techniques before training.

📦 MLflow Experiment Tracking

MLflow was integrated to:

Track experiments
Compare model versions
Log parameters
Log evaluation metrics
Store artifacts

Run MLflow UI:

mlflow ui

Access:

http://localhost:5000
🌐 REST API

The trained model is exposed using Flask.

Health Check
GET /health

Response:

{
  "status": "ok"
}
Prediction Endpoint
POST /predict

Sample Request:

{
  "from": "Brasilia",
  "to": "Natal",
  "flightType": "economic"
}

Sample Response:

{
  "predicted_price": 719.43,
  "currency": "BRL"
}
🎨 Frontend

The frontend provides:

Route selection
Flight type selection
Price prediction display
User-friendly visualization

This allows non-technical users to interact with the machine learning model.

🔄 Apache Airflow

Airflow was implemented to automate ML workflows.

DAG Responsibilities
Trigger training jobs
Execute model retraining
Manage workflow scheduling
Monitor execution status

Run Airflow:

docker compose up

Access:

http://localhost:8080
🐳 Dockerization

The application is fully containerized.

Build Image:

docker build -t flight-price-api .

Run Container:

docker run -p 5000:5000 flight-price-api
☸️ Kubernetes Deployment

The project is deployed using Kubernetes on Minikube.

Deployment
kubectl apply -f k8s/deployment.yaml
Service
kubectl apply -f k8s/service.yaml
Verify
kubectl get pods
kubectl get services
Access Application
minikube service flight-price-service --url
🔧 Jenkins CI/CD Pipeline

The Jenkins pipeline automates:

Source code checkout
Dependency installation
Model training
Docker image build
Docker image push
Kubernetes deployment

Pipeline definition:

Jenkinsfile

Benefits:

Faster deployments
Automated testing
Reproducible builds
Reduced manual effort
🛠️ Installation
Clone Repository
git clone <repository-url>
cd flightpriceapi
Create Virtual Environment
python -m venv venv
Activate Environment

Windows:

venv\Scripts\activate

Linux/Mac:

source venv/bin/activate
Install Dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
▶️ Run Locally
Train Model
python train_model.py
Start API
python app.py

Application:

http://localhost:5000
